Rāma finds tearful speechless father with Kaikēyī --- Rāma asks Kaikēyī for cause and pledges obedience --- Kaikēyī names Bharata crown and fourteen-year exile --- Rāma accepts bark locks and forest dwelling --- Rāma urges fetching Bharata and comforts father --- Kaikēyī demands departure before king bathes or eats --- Daśaratha faints wailing on golden couch --- Rāma reaffirms father obedience and exits unshaken --- Lakṣmaṇa follows tearful raging behind Rāma --- Rāma circles consecration gear and seeks mother